  "description": "ENOYOW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H114 Ce4 Mn2 N4 O34,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.268-4.094 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.22-136.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C56H114Ce4Mn2N4O34·4MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV), Mn(IV).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
